    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_f63649dd",
      "@type": "OverallIntent",
      "instance_name": "overallintent_instance",
      "label": "the overallintent",
      "description": "meme-id: meme_image; hasOverallIntent: harmful; overall-intent-description: The image features a man with a cigar in his mouth, juxtaposed with text that reads: 'you can make jokes about anything, just not illegals that's crossing the border.' This meme uses a visual of a stereotypical 'wise' or 'serious' man to deliver a message that humorously or sarcastically suggests that jokes about illegal immigration are taboo. The intent is to provoke thought or commentary on the topic of immigration and border control, but it does so by invoking a harmful stereotype — specifically, the association of immigrants with criminality and illegality — which is a well-documented form of anti-Latino/hispanic prejudice. The meme's overall intent is to be provocative and potentially inflammatory, using the juxtaposition of the image and text to reinforce a negative, fear-based narrative about immigrants, which can contribute to xenophobia and social division. The meme is harmful because it normalizes and spreads a prejudiced viewpoint that can lead to discrimination and hostility toward immigrant communities.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_aff7e1f5"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
